{"maxId":0,"entries":{"copy|Saliva plays an important protective role and contains a broad spectrum of antiviral, antibacterial, and antifungal proteins":["u74"],"copy|that modulate oral microbial colonization.":["u76"],"copy|With the current trends toward increasing tooth retention in aging populations,":["u85"],"copy|there is a correspondingly greater risk for the development of both of these disease entities.":["u90"],"copy|Long-standing dental caries ultimately result in the destruction of the tooth with the possibility of local or disseminated infection in the maxillofacial tissues, space infections in the head":["u111"],"copy|and neck, and infection in the systemic circulation (septicemia).":["u115"],"copy|Among healthy adults, periodontal attachment loss occurs at small increments in all age cohorts and does not occur in":["u135"],"copy|greater amounts in older healthy adults.":["u138"],"copy|Because acinar components are primarily responsible for the secretion of saliva, it is not known why, in the presence of a significant reduction in the gland acinar volume, total fluid production does":["u169"],"copy|not diminish with increasing age.":["u171"],"copy|Clinical examination includes palpation of all major":["u181"],"copy|glands and inspection of the duct orifices while milking the glands to ensure gland patency.":["u184"],"copy|Drugs":["u254"],"copy|used in older patients for arthritic conditions, hypertension, cardiac arrhythmias, seizures, and dementia are associated with lichenoid-like reactions.":["u256"],"copy|For lesions that are suspected to be oral manifestations of autoimmune connective tissue disorders (eg, pemphigus, pemphigoid,":["u262"],"copy|lichen planus), biopsies should also include specimens for direct immunofluorescence.":["u269"],"copy|There are important disparities in access to dental care, tooth loss, unfilled caries, periodontal diseases, and":["u340"],"copy|oral cancers among the poor, near poor, and racial and ethnic minorities.":["u351"],"copy|The interdisciplinary team working together can ensure":["u373"],"copy|that the needs of the patient are addressed in a timely and thorough manner.":["u390"],"copy|Premedication is often considered for patients with risk for endocarditis, autoimmune":["u394"],"copy|disease, chemotherapy, joint replacement, or heart murmurs.":["u398"],"copy|Oral health care should ideally be":["u418"],"copy|practiced in the morning when the patient wakes up, after each meal, and at their hour of sleep.":["u419"],"copy|TABLE 32-7 ■ TOP 10 ORAL HEALTH OUTCOMES IN LONG-TERM CARE":["u419"],"copy|In some cases, patients are not able to gain access to care at each of these points in a day due to the lack of available assistance.":["u420"]},"preservedBreaks":{"Saliva plays an important protective role and contains a broad spectrum of antiviral, antibacterial, and antifungal proteins that modulate oral microbial colonization.":[124],"With the current trends toward increasing tooth retention in aging populations, there is a correspondingly greater risk for the development of both of these disease entities.":[79],"Long-standing dental caries ultimately result in the destruction of the tooth with the possibility of local or disseminated infection in the maxillofacial tissues, space infections in the head and neck, and infection in the systemic circulation (septicemia).":[192],"Among healthy adults, periodontal attachment loss occurs at small increments in all age cohorts and does not occur in greater amounts in older healthy adults.":[117],"Because acinar components are primarily responsible for the secretion of saliva, it is not known why, in the presence of a significant reduction in the gland acinar volume, total fluid production does not diminish with increasing age.":[200],"Clinical examination includes palpation of all major glands and inspection of the duct orifices while milking the glands to ensure gland patency.":[52],"Drugs used in older patients for arthritic conditions, hypertension, cardiac arrhythmias, seizures, and dementia are associated with lichenoid-like reactions.":[5],"For lesions that are suspected to be oral manifestations of autoimmune connective tissue disorders (eg, pemphigus, pemphigoid, lichen planus), biopsies should also include specimens for direct immunofluorescence.":[126],"There are important disparities in access to dental care, tooth loss, unfilled caries, periodontal diseases, and oral cancers among the poor, near poor, and racial and ethnic minorities.":[112],"The interdisciplinary team working together can ensure that the needs of the patient are addressed in a timely and thorough manner.":[54],"Premedication is often considered for patients with risk for endocarditis, autoimmune disease, chemotherapy, joint replacement, or heart murmurs.":[85],"Oral health care should ideally be practiced in the morning when the patient wakes up, after each meal, and at their hour of sleep.":[34],"TABLE 32-7 ■ TOP 10 ORAL HEALTH OUTCOMES IN LONG-TERM CARE In some cases, patients are not able to gain access to care at each of these points in a day due to the lack of available assistance.":[58]},"sequenceOffsets":[[74,1],[75,2],[83,3],[87,4],[107,5],[110,6],[129,7],[131,8],[161,9],[162,10],[171,11],[173,12],[242,13],[243,14],[248,15],[254,16],[324,17],[334,18],[355,19],[371,20],[374,21],[377,22],[396,25]]}
